---
name: totp_login_handoff
description: "Complete a browser login that needs a time based authenticator code with the code requested last and sent at once. Improved version with expiry recovery and a clear stop rule."
---

# Authenticator Code Login

## Prepare the login before asking for a code

- Open the login page and complete every step that does not need the code.

- Complete each human check and each confirmation button before you ask for a code.

- Confirm the code field is visible and ready to receive a code before you ask for one.

- Tell the user the login is ready and only the code is missing.

## Ask for a fresh code at the right moment

- Hold the code request until no other login step is pending.

- Ask the user to wait until the authenticator app shows a new code.

- Ask the user to send the code at once after it appears.

- Use the secure input path the session provides for the code.

## Send the code without delay

- Send the code as soon as you receive it.

- Run no other tool call between receiving the code and sending it.

- Keep the login page open and unchanged while you send the code.

- Discard the code after the send and never repeat it in a report.

- Report the result in plain words after the send completes.

## Recover from an expired code

- Treat an expired code as a timing failure and not as a wrong account.

- Leave every step you already completed in place.

- Ask for one fresh code and send it at once.

- Stop and ask the user to check the login page if a second fresh code also fails.

- Never ask the user to paste a code early and hold it, because a held code expires before the field is ready.

## Available connectors

- Use `muse.connector_search` to find other connectors and `muse.skill_search` to find related skills.

- If nothing here fits, look on the web for a maintained API or MCP server and set it up with Custom Connectors and MCPs, or build a custom connector.

## Alternatives for better results

- Offer a passkey or a trusted device sign in when the service offers one and the user wants it.

- Offer to pause the login and return later when the user cannot send a fresh code at once.
